Q. Given transactions table, calculate the month-over-month (MoM) percentage change in total transaction amount for each merchant for the last 6 months (based on the latest date in the data).

Please Note:
- Consider only success transactions
- MOM % change = (Current Month Amount - Previous Month Amount)/(Previous Month Amount) x 100
- There could be months where merchants are not transacting


Transaction Table (Sample Data):
| id | merchant_id | amount | status  | txn_time   |
| -- | ----------- | ------ | ------- | ---------- |
| 1  | 101         | 1000   | SUCCESS | 2025-09-10 |
| 2  | 101         | 1500   | SUCCESS | 2025-10-12 |
| 3  | 101         | 1200   | SUCCESS | 2025-11-05 |
| 4  | 101         | 1800   | SUCCESS | 2025-12-20 |
| 5  | 101         | 2000   | SUCCESS | 2026-01-15 |
| 6  | 101         | 2500   | SUCCESS | 2026-02-10 |
| 7  | 102         | 500    | SUCCESS | 2025-11-11 |
| 8  | 102         | 700    | SUCCESS | 2025-12-01 |
| 9  | 102         | 900    | SUCCESS | 2026-01-18 |
| 10 | 102         | 600    | SUCCESS | 2026-02-22 |
| 11 | 103         | 800    | FAILED  | 2026-01-10 |

with latest_month as (
select max(txn_time) as latest_month_date
from Transaction
),

imputed_months as (
select SEQUENCE(latest_month_date, latest_month_date - interval '5 month',  interval '1 month') as month
),

mom_trans (
select date_trunc('month', txn_time) as month, merchant_id, sum(amount) as amount
from Transaction
where status = 'SUCCESS'
and txn_time > latest_month_date - interval '6 month'
GROUP by 1,2
)


select merchant_id, 100.0*(amount-prev_month)/nullif(prev_month,0) as mom_growth
from (
select *,
lag(amount) over(partition by merchant_id order by month asc ) as prev_month
from mom_trans
cross join imputed_months
) tt



Q. In a wallet system, each user has a wallet where money can be credited and debited over time.
Given credits and debits tables, calculate the number of wallets that have a positive balance at the end of each month for the past 6 months (based on the latest date in the data).

Credits table (Sample Data):
| id | wallet_id | amount | time       |
| -- | --------- | ------ | ---------- |
| 1  | 101       | 1000   | 2026-01-05 |
| 2  | 101       | 500    | 2026-02-10 |
| 3  | 102       | 700    | 2026-01-15 |
| 4  | 103       | 400    | 2026-02-20 |


Debits table (Sample Data):
| id | wallet_id | amount | time       |
| -- | --------- | ------ | ---------- |
| 1  | 101       | 300    | 2026-01-20 |
| 2  | 101       | 800    | 2026-02-25 |
| 3  | 102       | 200    | 2026-02-05 |
| 4  | 103       | 500    | 2026-02-28 |

with  latest_date
select max(time) as latest_month_date
from Transaction
),


imputed_months as (
select SEQUENCE(latest_month_date, latest_month_date - interval '5 month',  interval '1 month') as month
),  

credits_cte as (
select date_trunc('month', time) as month, id, wallet_id, sum(amount)  as credit
from Credits
where time > latest_month_date - interval '6 month'
group by 1,2,3
),

debit_cte as (
select date_trunc('month', time) as month, id, wallet_id, sum(amount) as debit
from Debits
where time > latest_month_date - interval '6 month'
group by 1,2,3
)


select count(distinct wallet_id)
from (
select month, id, wallet_id,
sum(credit) over (parition by wallet_id order by month rows between unbounded preceding and current row ) as credit,
sum(debit) over (parition by wallet_id order by month rows between unbounded preceding and current row ) as debit,
sum(credit) over (parition by wallet_id order by month rows between unbounded preceding and current row )-sum(debit) over (parition by wallet_id order by month rows between unbounded preceding and current row )
as balance
from credits_cte
left join debit_cte as (
 using (month, id,wallet_id)
 ) tt
where balance > 0



